  "id": "COMPOUND:29888 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link between 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and RWLeu4, mediated through a series of enzymatic targets. The compound is directly linked to the sialyltransferase CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one. These compounds are both targets of 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, and all of them ultimately target RWLeu4. This suggests a pathway where 2-Methylheptyl propanoate may inhibit the sialyltransferase enzyme, leading to a downstream effect on RWLeu4. The consistent presence of a target relationship across multiple compounds supports a plausible mechanism, though the exact nature of the inhibition and its relevance to RWLeu4 remains to be fully elucidated.",
